=== rocprofv3 --help (trace options) ===
  -i INPUT, --input INPUT               Input file for run configuration (JSON or YAML) or counter collection (TXT)
  -E EXTRA_COUNTERS, --extra-counters EXTRA_COUNTERS
                                        Path to YAML file containing extra counter definitions
  -r [BOOL], --runtime-trace [BOOL]     Collect tracing data for HIP runtime API, Marker (ROCTx) API, RCCL API, rocDecode API, rocJPEG API, Memory operations (copies, scratch, and allocation), and Kernel dispatches. Similar to --sys-trace but without tracing HIP compiler API and the underlying HSA API.
  -s [BOOL], --sys-trace [BOOL]         Collect tracing data for HIP API, HSA API, Marker (ROCTx) API, RCCL API, rocDecode API, rocJPEG API, Memory operations (copies, scratch, and allocations), and Kernel dispatches.
  --kernel-trace [BOOL]                 For collecting Kernel Dispatch Traces
  --memory-copy-trace [BOOL]            For collecting Memory Copy Traces. This was part of HIP and HSA traces in previous rocprof versions but is now a separate option
  --hsa-trace [BOOL]                    For collecting --hsa-core-trace, --hsa-amd-trace,--hsa-image-trace and --hsa-finalizer-trace. This option only enables the tracing of the HSA API. Unlike previous iterations of rocprof, this does not enable kernel tracing, memory copy tracing, etc
  --hsa-core-trace [BOOL]               For collecting HSA API Traces (core API), e.g. HSA functions prefixed with only 'hsa_' (i.e. hsa_init).
  --hsa-amd-trace [BOOL]                For collecting HSA API Traces (AMD-extension API), e.g. HSA function prefixed with 'hsa_amd_' (i.e. hsa_amd_coherency_get_type).
  --hsa-image-trace [BOOL]              For collecting HSA API Traces (Image-extension API), e.g. HSA functions prefixed with only 'hsa_ext_image_' (i.e. hsa_ext_image_get_capability).
  --hsa-finalizer-trace [BOOL]          For collecting HSA API Traces (Finalizer-extension API), e.g. HSA functions prefixed with only 'hsa_ext_program_' (i.e. hsa_ext_program_create).
Counter collection options:
  --pmc [PMC ...]                       Specify Performance Monitoring Counters to collect(comma OR space separated in case of more than 1 counters). Note: job will fail if entire set of counters cannot be collected in single pass
  --stats [BOOL]                        For collecting statistics of enabled tracing types. Must be combined with one or more tracing options. No default kernel stats unlike previous rocprof versions
                                        Output a summary for each set of domains matching the regular expression, e.g. 'KERNEL_DISPATCH|MEMORY_COPY' will generate a summary from all the tracing data in the KERNEL_DISPATCH and MEMORY_COPY domains; '*._API' will generate a summary from all the tracing data in the HIP_API, HSA_API, and MARKER_API domains
                                        Include the kernels matching this filter from counter-collection and thread-trace data (non-matching kernels will be excluded)
                                        Exclude the kernels matching this filter from counter-collection and thread-trace data (applied after --kernel-include-regex option)
  -L [BOOL], --list-avail [BOOL]        List available PC sampling configurations and metrics for counter collection. Backed by a valid YAML file. In earlier rocprof versions, this was known as --list-basic, --list-derived and --list-counters
  --group-by-queue [BOOL]               For displaying the HIP streams that kernels and memory copy operations are submitted to rather than HSA queues.
